# Deliberately short. This is a coursework repository, not a software project,
# so the rule is: ignore what a tool generates, never ignore what you might
# submit. Nothing here matches *.pdf, *.png, *.jpg, or *.md — your writeups,
# figures, and exported reports are meant to be committed.

# --- Ansys / CAD scratch --------------------------------------------------
# Workbench writes a multi-gigabyte sibling directory next to every .wbpj.
# Committing one will exhaust GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit and wedge your
# repository. If a lab asks you to hand in a model, export or archive it
# (.wbpz) and check that single file in deliberately.
*_files/
*.mechdb
*.mechdat
*.dsdb
*.lock
*.err
*.abt
# .rst/.rth are Ansys *result* files (often gigabytes), not reStructuredText.
# If you ever write documentation in .rst here, un-ignore it deliberately.
*.rst
*.rth
~$*

# SolidWorks / Inventor backup and lock files
*.SLDPRT.bak
*.SLDASM.bak
*.SLDDRW.bak
*.ipt.bak
*.iam.bak
*~

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
# For the calculation and plotting scripts you may keep alongside a problem set.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/

# --- Editors and OS ------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Secrets --------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing in this course needs an API key in your repository, and this repo may
# be visible to the teaching team. If you ever find yourself adding one, stop.
.env
*.pem
*_token
